.TH SIMRV-CONFIG-WIZARD 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-config-wizard \- create CPU and platform configurations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-config-wizard
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-config-wizard
creates CPU model configurations or imports a compiled flattened device tree (DTB) to create a
combined CPU/SoC configuration. With interactive terminals, it presents a simple text wizard and
allows review of imported values before writing the configuration. It also validates model or
platform configurations with \fB--validate\fR. The historic
.B simrv-cpu-wizard
name remains available as a compatibility alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-from-dtb \fIPATH\fR
Import platform details from a compiled DTB.
.TP
.B \-\-validate \fIFILE|PRESET\fR
Validate a CPU model or platform configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Set the output configuration name. The default is \fBcustom_riscv\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-template \fIPRESET\fR, \-\-preset \fIPRESET\fR
Choose the CPU model preset: \fBbalanced\fR, \fBtiny\fR, \fBperformance\fR.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Write the configuration to this path. By default it is written below \fBconfigs/models/\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Generate without presenting the terminal review UI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1)
